email.task:
You are an IT officer. Sara, the office manager, has asked you for information about the company's new wireless network so that she can tell all the staff. Write an email to Sara using the notes below. In your email you must use:
- the present continuous at least once for something that is happening now (The IT team is installing…);
- at least one relative clause with which, that or who;
- at least one zero conditional sentence (If + present simple, present simple: If a visitor uses Bridge-Guest, they don't see the server.) or first conditional sentence (If + present simple, will + verb: If you use the old network after Friday, it won't work.).
Write 80–100 words.
